or stored the request’s records."}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"outcome"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"of"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"response"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations21HTTPTransportResponseV","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransportResponse","text":"HTTPTransportResponse"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"for"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"request"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations14EncodedRequestV","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedRequest","text":"EncodedRequest"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations15ResponseOutcomeO","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ResponseOutcome","text":"ResponseOutcome"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"response","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The answer: a 2xx status, its header fields and its body.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"request","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The request it answers, as the encoder made it."}]}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Return Value","level":2,"anchor":"return-value"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether the request’s records were delivered, refused for good, or refused for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"now."}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" calls it for every 2xx answer, and only for those, with the answer’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"status, header fields and body, and the request it answers, for a vendor whose answer is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"read against what was sent (a count of the records it took, say). An encoder for a vendor that stores what it answers 2xx to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"returns "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ResponseOutcome\/delivered"},{"type":"text","text":". One for a vendor that answers 2xx to a request it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stores nothing of, and says so in the body (Mixpanel’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{\"status\": 0, \"error\": ...}"},{"type":"text","text":"),"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"returns "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ResponseOutcome\/rejected(reason:)"},{"type":"text","text":", which drops and reports the request, or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ResponseOutcome\/transient(reason:)"},{"type":"text","text":", which sends it again. A body the vendor doesn’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"document, an empty one or one that doesn’t parse included, is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ResponseOutcome\/delivered"},{"type":"text","text":": the request did arrive, and sending it again after an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"answer the encoder can’t read would repeat it for as long as the vendor keeps answering"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that way. The conformance kit’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"unreadableSuccessDelivered"},{"type":"text","text":" check holds an encoder to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this. An encoder that wraps another forwards the wrapped encoder’s outcome."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A transient outcome is sent again until it is delivered, rejected, or past the request’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedRequest\/deadline"},{"type":"text","text":". A request with no deadline is sent again for as long as the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vendor keeps answering that way, so an encoder whose requests have none returns"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ResponseOutcome\/rejected(reason:)"},{"type":"text","text":" rather than "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ResponseOutcome\/transient(reason:)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"unless the vendor documents that the answer passes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A vendor fact, as "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder\/transientStatuses","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is, so it is static, with no default: a conformer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that leaves it out, or misspells it, doesn’t compile, rather than silently counting a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"refused request as delivered."}]}]}],"kind":"symbol","references